//! A tiny cross-platform utility crate that demonstrates a clean pattern for
//! conditional compilation.
//!
//! # Design
//!
//! `#[cfg]` attributes are a powerful but easy-to-mismanage part of Rust. When
//! target checks are sprinkled through a codebase they become hard to audit and
//! easy to get out of sync, and mistakes only show up when you compile for the
//! platform you forgot about.
//!
//! This crate keeps that complexity in one place:
//!
//! * [`sys`] owns the *only* target-dispatch table in the crate. It selects a
//!   single backend module — `linux`, `macos`, `windows`, `wasm`, or a generic
